## Why This Is Asked
This question probes low-level memory allocator design under NUMA, testing correctness, performance, and testability in a kernel-like environment.

## Key Concepts
- NUMA-aware caches and per-node freelists
- Lock-free transfer and CAS-based synchronization
- Refill thresholds and batch transfers
- Fragmentation management and performance under contention
- Benchmarking tail latency with CPU pinning and mixed I/O

## Code Example
```c
// Minimal sketch of allocation path
struct slab_cache { // per-size cache
  struct atomic_head local_head;
  // ... remote/mempool refs
};
void* slab_alloc(struct slab_cache* cache, int size) {
  void* obj = atomic_pop(&cache->local_head);
  if (obj) return obj;
  obj = steal_batch(cache, size); // remote/global refill
  return obj;
}
```

